theory.intro:
A non-unit fraction such as $\tfrac{2}{5}$ has a numerator greater than $1$. Find it by first finding one part, then taking that many copies.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"fractionBlueFill","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Identify selected equal fractional parts of the whole; restrained mathematical fraction shading."}],"reference":"Preserve all equal-part geometry and labels; ordinary black strokes; selected fraction fill uses standard palette"}
\definecolor{fractionBlueFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.9cm,every node/.style={font=\small}]
\fill[fractionBlueFill] (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,1);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (0,1.15)--(2,1.15);
\node[above] at (1,1.35) {shaded parts};
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,mirror,amplitude=5pt}] (0,-0.15)--(5,-0.15);
\node[below] at (2.5,-0.35) {the whole quantity};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A tape represents a total quantity of $80$. It is split into five equal sections.
Find the quantity represented by the three shaded sections.
[tikz]% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"templateShade","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Identify the three selected fifths of the given whole quantity."}],"reference":"template nonunit-tape-question"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\definecolor{templateShade}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\path[use as bounding box] (-0.6,-10.6) rectangle (25.6,0.6);
\fill[templateShade] (0,-10) rectangle (5,0);
\fill[templateShade] (5,-10) rectangle (10,0);
\fill[templateShade] (10,-10) rectangle (15,0);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (5,0)--(5,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (10,0)--(10,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (15,0)--(15,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (20,0)--(20,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (25,-10);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Find $\frac{2}{5}$ of $30$.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"fractionBlueFill","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Identify selected equal fractional parts of the whole; restrained mathematical fraction shading."}],"reference":"Preserve all equal-part geometry and labels; ordinary black strokes; selected fraction fill uses standard palette"}
\definecolor{fractionBlueFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}

\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.8cm]
\fill[fractionBlueFill] (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,1);}
\node[above] at (2.5,1) {total $30$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

